export anchor LabInstrumentStyle:
    number: 72
    screen: TodayMobile
    name: Lab instrument
    idea: The phone becomes a bench instrument with a screwed chassis, inset readouts on graph paper, tasks logged as labelled samples and meetings plotted on a time axis.
    base: light
    palette:
        bench: #dfe3e1, the page around the device
        chassis: #eef0ee, the device body and panel headers
        graph: #f8fbf7, readout and panel paper and fields
        gridMajor: #c5d8cb, major graph lines every 40px, decorative only
        gridMinor: #e2ece5, minor graph lines every 8px, decorative only
        ink: #1a2626, text, axes and readout figures
        graphite: #4b5a59, engraved labels, units and the Queued flag
        bezel: #8d9896, panel, sample and field edges
        traceGreen: #0b6e4f, the add key, primary button, Done and the power light
        probeBlue: #0e5f86, Due today, meeting blocks and focus
        alarmRed: #b02a1e, Overdue with a cross, the hatched sample tab and the badge
        caution: #f5c542, the High priority tag with #4a3500 text
    type:
        Monospace ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Cascadia Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas for every value, 26px bold readout counts with small unit
        letters, 20px bold for the date, 16px bold meeting times and 11 to
        12px meta with units and deltas. Engineering sans DIN Alternate,
        Bahnschrift, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Arial for names and labels,
        15px semibold task names and 9 to 11px heavy caps engraved labels
        tracked 0.18 to 0.2em.
    layout:
        A device body up to 396px centred on the bench, with four corner
        screws. An engraved plate holds a green power light, Brightwork,
        Daily analyser and a square avatar. Below it an inset readout shows
        Run date Monday 2 November and large Tasks 6 and Meetings 2 counts,
        with 6 tasks, 2 meetings as a small line. Two graph-paper panels
        follow. Scheduled runs has a time axis plot from 8 to 16 h with the
        two meetings as blocks, then two run rows with time, name and a
        delta length. Samples has a due date plot with error bars, a now
        line and one marker per sample, then six sample labels each with a
        6px coloured tab, an id such as S-01 and a project code, the name,
        the project and due date with a day delta, and a status flag. A
        control strip of round knob tabs and a square green add key ends
        the device.
    spacing: A 4px base on an 8px graph grid. 12px between panels, 8px between samples, 6 to 10px padding.
    density: Dense but ordered. Every value carries a unit or a delta.
    corners: 2 to 6px like softened metal. Knobs and screws are round.
    borders: 1px bezel lines everywhere. Sample labels have a 6px tab, hatched red and white for overdue. The current knob gets a 2px ink ring and a small triangle pointer below.
    shadows: Inset 0 1px 3px for readouts and fields, a white top highlight and a 2px hard bottom edge for the chassis and keys.
    icons:
        1.8 stroke line icons inside round knob discs, with a flask for
        Projects. Status flags pair a word with a filled dot for Due today,
        a hollow ring for Queued, a tick for Done and a cross for Overdue.
        High priority is a yellow caution tag with a triangle.
    focus: A 2px probe blue outline offset 2px plus a soft 5px blue halo.
    tone: Measured and technical, such as Runs, Samples, Queued, Δt 30 min and +2 d.
